  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Venezuela crisis 2021 - WFP HUM 2019-2021 (HUM strategy 2021-2025)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser humanit&#xe4;rt st&#xf6;d genom World Food Program (WFP) f&#xf6;r perioden 2019-2021. WFP har varit en regelbunden partner f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;randet av Sidas humanit&#xe4;ra insatser senast genom ett fler&#xe5;rigt avtal f&#xf6;r perioden 2015-2017, samt ett avtal f&#xf6;r 2018. Det f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;s nu att &#xe5;terigen ing&#xe5; ett tre&#xe5;rigt avtal f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka f&#xf6;ruts&#xe4;gbarhet och flexibilitet i samarbetet. Av 2019 &#xe5;rs st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida, totalt 151 MSEK, avses 96 MSEK att anv&#xe4;ndas f&#xf6;r WFP:s huvudverksamhet varav 90 MSEK till akuta mats&#xe4;kerhetsinsatser och 6 MSEK till kapacitetsst&#xf6;d. Resterande 55 MSEK avses anv&#xe4;ndas till finansiering av United Nations Humanitarian Air Services (UNHAS) f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra tilltr&#xe4;de till m&#xe4;nniskor i behov av humanit&#xe4;r hj&#xe4;lp.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution entails humanitarian support through the World Food Program (WFP) for the period 2019-2021. WFP has been a regular partner for the implementation of Sida&apos;s humanitarian assistance through a multi-year agreement for the period 2015-2017, and an agreement for 2018. It is hereby proposed to enter into a new three-year agreement to increase predictability and flexibility of the cooperation. Of 2019 years&apos; support from Sida, amounting to a total of 151 million SEK, 96 million SEK will be distributed for WFP&apos;s core activities, including 90 MSEK for emergency food security interventions and 6 MSEK for capacity strengthening, while the remaining SEK 55 million will be used to finance the United Nations Humanitarian Air Services (UNHAS) to improve access to people in need of humanitarian aid.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this contribution is to provide life-saving assistance to people affected by food insecurity and malnutrition through support to WFP&apos;s humanitarian operations in a number of countries, annually identified by Sida&apos;s humanitarian Unit during the course of the allocation process or as a response to sudden changes in the humanitarian situation in-country. The contribution from Sida will mainly be used for (i) food assistance, (ii) targeted nutrition interventions and (iii) transport and logistics on behalf of the whole humanitarian community.</narrative>
  </description>
